WEBVTT

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.140
Kai-kun!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.610
What is it?

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.200
Oh, never mind.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.490
Sorry, I think I got the wrong person.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.700
Hi there, welcome back.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.190
Manager Nitta?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.210
You seem to be having fun.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.960
Yes, I am!

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.070
But before, you seemed oddly dejected.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.090
Like you'd been stood up by your girlfriend!

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.860
W-Wait, that's not it at all!

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.430
Kai-kun wasn't here, so I...

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.220
Now that you mention it, he hasn't 
been here for a couple days, has he?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.330
Well, you can never tell with him.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.800
But why do you want to see him so badly?

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.630
I want to have another 
Vanguard Fight with Kai.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.020
The first time I fought with Kai, I 
had a feeling he was holding back.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.560
Because I'd never played before...

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.720
But since then, I've had numerous fights,

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.730
learned how to play Vanguard, 
and it's gotten more fun!

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.730
Plus maybe, just maybe, I've gotten better.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:01.220
So I want to face Kai once 
again with my newfound power!

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.660
Your eyes are really sparkling, Aichi.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.210
Everyone is like that in the beginning.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:13.300
It's always fun and engrossing... Losing 
is the farthest thing from one's mind.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.720
Would you show me your deck?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.130
Uh... Okay.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.350
Is something the matter?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.870
Okay, let's do this.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.140
After school tomorrow, come to the shop.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.900
There'll be something nice 
waiting for you there, I bet.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.900
Something nice?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.530
Yes! Make sure to come, okay?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.370
Assault! Twin Drive!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.140
Somethin' nice!

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.860
Aichi, what's the "something nice"?

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.920
I asked <i>you</i> because I didn't know!

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.550
We're here!

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.000
Okay then, what's this nice thing you got?

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.390
Why don't you share some of it with me, eh?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.270
Please keep quiet while inside the shop.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.110
I see you came, Aichi.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:14.890
Yes.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:18.570
Manager! What's this "nice 
thing" you got for Aichi, huh?

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.110
To find that out, I'd like you 
to have a Vanguard fight first.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.680
A cardfight?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.330
Yes. After that fight is over, I'm sure 
you'll begin to notice something nice.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.000
Then fight me, too!

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.680
I think you're good already, Morikawa.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.860
It's Aichi who needs to see it...

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.670
What are you talking about?

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.290
So yeah... I was planning 
on playing you myself,

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.750
but there's this sudden meeting 
for the local shops...

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:51.020
In my place, I'd like you to fight Misaki.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.970
"Uwah!" is my line!

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.010
Me? Fight this guy?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.610
Yes.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.180
Shin, you can't just tell me to...

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.670
Ahem... Please call me "Manager".

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.050
Whatever! You know, right?

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.040
You know I've never had 
a Vanguard Fight before!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.820
But you're always here manning the shop!

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.560
I just help out here with 
Shin's shop, that's all.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.710
I have no interest in cardfights.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.720
"Manager"?

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.740
What will I be able to see in this fight?

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.380
Were you just teasing me?

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.260
You'll know if you try.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.660
I'm not teasing you.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.240
Uh, oh! I'm going to be late for the meeting.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.130
Please use this deck.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.340
But...

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.570
I'm sure you'll be fine, Misaki.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.960
And? What are we going to do about here?

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:52.040
While I'm having a Vanguard Fight, 
who will watch the counter?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.530
Oh, yeah...

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.930
In that case...

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.250
We'll use the Sub-Manager!

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:02.790
Seriously?

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.600
Howdy!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.040
Oh?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.880
So the manager said that?

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.490
That's why we've got the 
two of them like this.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.250
Then, what's that guy doing?

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.000
Can't you tell?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:26.920
Actually, no.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:31.960
I'm sure you can only see the nice 
thing the manager mentioned if you win!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.030
So I'm praying!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.650
Aichi... lose!

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.510
How dare you hog the nice stuff to yourself!

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.790
Ouch.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.280
So it's <i>this</i> kind of deck...

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.440
I wonder what Shin is thinking, though?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:51.300
He's totally buying me another 2 
or 3 outfits in exchange for this.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.090
She's never had a fight before,

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.790
so maybe I should go a bit easy on her?

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:57.950
Let's begin.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:58.810
Right!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.610
Sorry, let me shuffle again...

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.590
S-Sure.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.690
She's not used to handling cards...

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.010
Please cut my deck.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.150
Picture it.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:38.940
Right.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.040
Vanguard, stand up!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.740
Lozenge Magus.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.030
Stardust Trumpeter.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.010
I go first.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:14.130
I ride Oracle Guardian Gemini.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:23.130
Using the effect of Lozenge Magus, 
he moves himself to the rear guard.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:28.310
Yup, she's green! Awkward...

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.740
We're in the middle of a fight!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.800
I'm sorry...

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:33.220
It's your turn.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.510
I ride the Little Sage, Marron.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.620
And call Wingal and Flogal.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.100
I combine Flogal's power with 
Wingal's, and attack Gemini!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.590
Check for a damage trigger.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.690
Next, I attack Gemini with Marron!

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.450
Check for a drive trigger...

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:13.370
Got it!

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:14.820
Drive trigger!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.630
From Epona's effect, Marron's 
power gains 5000 additional power.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:22.840
And the effect of a critical 
trigger increases damage by 1!

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.950
I took 2 damage then, yes?

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.790
Then I can also check for triggers twice.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.670
First check for a damage trigger...

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.290
Got it. Draw trigger.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:35.270
Draw trigger?

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:39.000
The effect of this is that I 
can draw a card, I believe.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.940
Now, checking the second damage trigger...

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.310
Another draw trigger.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.280
Triggers that grow the size of your hand?

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.770
Is that actually helpful?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.620
3 cards in her damage zone right off the bat!

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.970
No mercy for the greenhorn, huh?

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.020
I must not be praying hard enough!

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.450
Aichi, don't you dare win!

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:04.740
Uh...

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:05.660
Shut up!

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.470
Righto...

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:08.840
We're sorry.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.220
It's my turn.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.490
I ride Maiden of Libra.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.640
And I call two Silent Toms.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.790
I attack Marron with Silent Tom.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.230
Then I guard with Flogal.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.860
No, you can't do that.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.300
Huh?

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.970
It's Silent Tom's skill.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.990
A grade 0 cannot guard his attack.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:42.980
Sorry 'bout that.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.010
There are attacks you can't guard against?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:06.110
Misaki might never have fought before, 
but she knows how to use the cards.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.720
I can't let my guard down!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.730
Not bad...

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.990
That's the way, girly! Get Aichi good!

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.490
I said shut up! We're fighting here!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.050
S-S-Sorry!

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.310
I still have the upper hand,

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:50.310
but I have to do something 
about those Silent Toms...

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.910
My turn!

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.400
All right!

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.530
Stand up, my avatar!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:03.190
Ride Blaster Blade!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.770
Blaster Blade Counter Blast!

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.830
I retire a Silent Tom!

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.920
That's one. Only one more.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.510
I continue by calling Flogal and Gallatin!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:35.200
I attack Maiden of Libra with Gallatin!

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.560
I guard with Oracle Guardian Nike.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.360
I'm not done yet!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.490
Blaster Blade borrows Flogal's 
power, and attacks Libra!

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.990
Drive Check!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.900
Check for a damage trigger...

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.820
Draw trigger.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:03.570
I draw a card because of the draw trigger.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.650
It's about time...

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:12.520
I give Flogal's power to 
Wingal, and attack Silent Tom!

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:21.500
All right! All the Silent Toms are gone!

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.490
Don't count your chickens just yet.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.860
We're only getting started.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:33.840
That's...

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.490
The beautiful Goddess, shining radiantly!

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:40.380
Ride CEO Amaterasu!

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.050
Amaterasu? A grade 3?

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.070
She had one of <i>those</i>?

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:55.570
The strongest cards in all of Vanguard!

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:56.810
Grade 3!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.560
You sure love your grade 3s...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.460
Heck yeah! They're the 
strongest, just like me!

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:03.470
Sure, whatever.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.030
Grade 3?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.280
I activate Amaterasu's skill.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.280
I lay my soul on the deck,

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:16.040
and check the card on top.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.250
Check the top card?

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:25.190
With this, I can look at the topmost card and 
decide to leave it on top or move it to the bottom.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.720
Is there some point to that?

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.330
You'll understand soon.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.140
I don't need this one.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:37.720
I call 2 Oracle Guardian 
Wisemen, and a Gemini.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:43.410
I attack Blaster Blade with Wiseman.

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.110
I guard with Epona!

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.310
I add Gemini's power to Wiseman,

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.270
and attack Blaster Blade.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.890
Check for a damage trigger...

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.120
Good. I got a heal trigger!

00:14:57.430 --> 00:15:01.560
Elaine's effect allows me to recover 
1 card from my damage zone!

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.050
No, you can't.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:09.140
You can only do that when the number of 
cards in your damage zone is more than mine.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.970
I can't recover!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:20.370
She knows about the cards 
and how fights work.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.280
Even though this is her first fight...

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:26.940
I'm sitting at the counter 
every day watching the shop.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.250
I'd have memorized them even without trying.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:34.670
And if I didn't, I wouldn't be 
able to serve the customers.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:38.500
I see. So that's why you 
know so much, Misaki.

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:41.460
But I still have an effect left!

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.780
Blaster Blade's power is +5000!

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.960
Now she can't attack carelessly.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.930
I attack Blaster Blade with Amaterasu.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.070
Huh? But, why?

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.310
Check for a drive trigger.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.800
Twin drive.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.350
Twin drive?

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:09.100
Grade three cards have an 
ability called "twin drive".

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:12.160
They can check for a drive trigger twice.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.530
First check...

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.980
Second check...

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.890
No triggers...

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:22.750
Phew...

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.350
Amaterasu has a certain ability...

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:30.710
When you have 4 or more cards in your 
hand, her power increases by 4000.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.080
Ah! She's got 5 cards in her hand!

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:36.970
I see, so that's why those 
draw triggers mattered...

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:41.000
It was to activity this 
ability of Amaterasu's!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.240
It's too late to realize it now.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:00.020
She's rackin' up the damage!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:03.740
Amaterasu... Yup, grade 3s are awesome!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.760
I ain't gonna lose!

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:09.450
I change Wingal for Flogal.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:14.230
Then, I retire Flogal and call Gallatin!

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.640
I attack Amaterasu with Gallatin!

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.020
I do not defend.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.590
One more point...

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:31.610
Okay! I give Flogal's power to 
Blaster Blade and attack Amaterasu!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.260
I guard with Chocolat.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.670
Skill activated.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:39.320
I drop an Oracle Guardian from my 
hand, which nullifies the attack.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:44.860
Attack nullified.

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.150
Chocolat goes to the drop zone.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.690
Check for a drive trigger...

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.080
Drive trigger activated!

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.750
From Epona's effect, power is +5000.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:02.850
I give Wingal's power to this 
Gallatin, and attack Amaterasu!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.510
Guard with Chocolat.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:16.790
But...

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:18.700
It's time to finish this...

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.380
I activate Amaterasu's skill.

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:24.580
I charge a soul, and check the deck.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.470
I don't need this one.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.180
I call Miracle Kid and Cocoa.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:40.480
Cocoa can check the deck, just like Amaterasu.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.400
I'll leave this one.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:50.010
I give Miracle Kid's power to 
Wiseman, and attack Blaster Blade!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.410
I guard with Epona.

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.620
I'll guard, no matter what you throw at me!

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:58.400
I power Wiseman with Gemini, and attack.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.250
I guard with Epona!

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:04.840
I power Amaterasu with Cocoa, 
and attack Blaster Blade!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:05.800
Amaterasu!

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.680
Oh, no!

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.090
I used up my entire hand!

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:17.540
Check for a driver trigger. Twin drive.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.670
First check.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:21.980
This is the card from before.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:27.190
The card she left on top 
after checking with Cocoa!

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:31.910
The purpose of checking the top card 
and deciding whether to leave it there,

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:35.440
is to enable you to anticipate 
getting a trigger.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.500
Drive trigger activated.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.990
Nike's effect adds +5000 to Amaterasu's power.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:46.420
And the critical trigger's 
effect adds +1 to the damage.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.760
Second check.

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:52.960
No trigger.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.480
However, now Amaterasu's power is 21000.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.550
This is the power of a grade 3.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:06.790
Yes... A deck with no more 
than grade 2s like yours,

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:09.360
will never win against it!

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.990
It's over.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:29.080
Aichi lost...

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:38.490
Grade 3s... Amazing.

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:41.910
I don't have anything like that in my deck.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:47.470
Lost to Misaki, I see?

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:49.160
Yes...

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.060
And?

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.860
Did you see something?

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:56.810
Yes... I saw that I still 
have a lot to learn.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:01.420
The world of Vanguard is much 
more vast than I thought.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:05.070
That's the nice thing I 
wanted to show you, Aichi.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:08.790
Everyone is the same:

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:13.290
When they start Vanguard, they only 
know their own little sliver of it.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.880
But if they stay that way, they 
never get any more skilled.

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:19.960
You'll never defeat Kai like that.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:24.390
Well, I'm glad you saw something nice.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:27.800
The vast world of Vanguard, huh?

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:31.010
Tch... Whatever.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.230
I know that all too well.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.610
What did you think it was?

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:37.490
Me? Something like...

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:43.580
Showing me a grade 3 that 
even I don't have yet!

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:46.900
Boasting, are we?

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:51.310
If you want to know about the 
cards, I'll teach you anytime.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:54.210
You mean as long as he comes to 
the store as a customer, right?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.710
Thank you very much!

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:02.170
Grade 3s...

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:05.360
And all those cards I've never seen before...

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:09.550
I want to know more about Vanguard, 
and get even stronger...

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:12.830
So that one day, with Kai...

00:23:51.140 --> 00:23:53.700
It was your first fight, Misaki.

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:56.240
Yeah, but I'm always watching 
them from the counter.

00:23:56.240 --> 00:24:00.120
Wow... I'm just happy being with everyone.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.700
I bet there are lots of strong 
people out there I haven't met yet!

00:24:03.700 --> 00:24:05.910
There's a powerful grade-schooler, you know.

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:06.960
Oh, really?

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:08.590
I'd like to meet him.

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:12.170
Wait, is that grade-school kid 
fighting Izaki right now...

00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:16.110
Next time: Whirlwind! Kamui, 
the Grade-School Fighter!

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:18.500
Picture it... Myself becoming stronger!
